r hand a  north korean dictator met twice and  shook hands with the president of the  united states himself something that had  never happened before these were truly  strange images meetings that of course  did not take long to blow up  the latest reproachment between north  korea the united states and south korea  took place in 2019 in the vietnamese  city of hanoi this summit was a real  fiasco after almost two years of  charades kim still had not achieved his  real goal to have sanctions against  north korea lifted and of course the  charade without any result was already  dragging on so long that it was  beginning to hurt kim's image the north  korean leader was showing an uncommon  image of weakness in the face of his own  regime let's just say that he had shaken  hands with his arch enemy to achieve  absolutely nothing  as a result the hanoi summit ended  prematurely and according to the united  states these were the reasons  it was all about the sanctions basically  they wanted the sanctions lifted in  their entirety and we couldn't do that  president donald trump  the dilemma that we were confronted with  is the north koreans at this point are  unwilling to impose a complete freeze on  their weapons of mass destruction  programmes so to give many many billions  of dollars in sanctions relief would in  effect put us in position of subsidizing  the ongoing development of weapons of  mass destruction in north korea senior  u.s state department official oh kim kim  they saw your play it was the snake that  bites its own tail north korea demanded  an end to sanctions before making any  gestures and the united states demanded  that north korea dismantle its nuclear  and ballistic program before lifting  anything it was clear that any agreement  was impossible so everything fell apart  and north korea's economic crisis  continued we have now come all the way  to 2019 and this is what happened next  listen up  kovid's final nail in the world's most  hermetic country  2019 was also a bad year for the kim  jong-un regime first the sanctions were  still in place and it was clear that  they were not going away so the north  korean leader no longer had any  incentive to continue to show a friendly  face for what so do you know what he did  well yes he went back to the policy of  reinforcing the armed forces at all  costs especially in terms of strategic  armaments he did it perhaps to present  himself once again as a tough and strong  guy to the regime's own top brass or  perhaps to make up for his political  failure or perhaps to remind the world  that kim jong-un was not some affable  good-natured guy be that as it may this  meant the end of the beyond jin doctrine  and a return to the old policies  in this way kim largely re-established  the usual economic system and returned  in his speeches to the importance of  self-sufficiency which basically means a  return to the hard and strict autarky  that had been so characteristic of north  korea and in terms of foreign policy kim  jong-un progressively froze all the  dialogues that had been opened in the  previous phase the most dramatic  expression of this was to blow up the k  song into korean liaison office in june  2020  and of course don't forget that late  2019 early 2020 was when the sars  coronavirus ii pandemic was set in  motion a pandemic which as we all know  originated in china and which caused the  regime to close down again practically  from the outset not even allowing trade  with china except for essential goods so  the north korean economy once again went  back into recession and given the  circumstances in this country what is  lost is not regained with kovite 19  north korea has returned to a state of  almost total isolation to a state of  absolute autarky and extreme crisis  something very similar or even worse  than what kim jong-un found when he  ascended to the throne in 2011.  and that is not all to make matters  worse the lack of water infrastructure  and h